## Core Capabilities

- Anti bot bypass for systems such as Cloudflare, DataDome, and Akamai.
- Proxy infrastructure managed by HasData, including residential and datacenter routing.
- JavaScript rendering and browser like page interaction.
- Structured extraction for search results, maps, reviews, listings, products, jobs, flights, and web pages.
- LLM ready outputs including Markdown for AI pipelines and RAG workflows.
- Automatic retries and billing focused on successful requests.

## Common Use Cases

- SEO monitoring: keyword rankings, SERP features, AI Overviews, and competitor visibility.
- Lead generation: company, listing, and contact data from search engines, maps, directories, and websites.
- Market research: prices, catalogs, reviews, search visibility, and trend monitoring.
- Local business data: listings, categories, addresses, phone numbers, ratings, reviews, and opening hours.
- Real estate data: property listings, prices, attributes, and market changes.
- Travel data: flight and accommodation data for travel products and analytics.
- AI and LLM workflows: public web content and structured data for RAG, enrichment, monitoring, and training.

## Industries

- SEO and search intelligence
- Lead generation and sales intelligence
- Market intelligence and competitive monitoring
- Local business data products
- Real estate and proptech
- Travel data products
- AI and LLM systems

## How HasData Works

HasData is the scraping infrastructure layer between your system and the target website.
You send a request to a HasData endpoint or run a scraper job.
HasData fetches the target page, handles browser execution and anti bot systems, and returns structured output.
This lets teams use web data without maintaining their own proxy, browser, and extraction stack.

## Integrations

HasData fits into developer workflows and AI workflows.
Common integrations and downstream tools include Python, Node.js, Zapier, Make, n8n, webhooks, GitHub based workflows, ChatGPT, LangChain, and LlamaIndex.

## Why Teams Choose HasData

- One platform for APIs, no code scrapers, datasets, and custom scraping.
- No need to operate proxy rotation, CAPTCHA solving, or browser fleet infrastructure in house.
- Outputs ready for analytics, applications, and AI systems.
- Public data focus with compliance oriented positioning.
- Free starting tier with 1,000 trial credits.
- Paid plans start at $59 per month.

## Differentiation

HasData is not just a proxy network or a no code tool.
HasData combines APIs, scrapers, datasets, and custom delivery in one platform.

