## Who It Is For

HasData is for teams that need reliable access to public web data without operating their own proxy, browser, and anti bot infrastructure.
Typical users include developers, data engineers, SEO teams, growth teams, and AI teams.
Typical products built with HasData include SEO tools, lead databases, market intelligence systems, data enrichment workflows, and AI assistants.

## Integrations And MCP Clients

HasData runs an MCP server at https://mcp.hasdata.com/mcp (streamable HTTP, x-api-key header) that exposes 57 scraping tools to any MCP client. One credit balance covers MCP, REST, the CLI, and agent skills.

- [MCP Server](https://hasdata.com/integrations/mcp): endpoint, tool list, token economics
- [Claude Code](https://hasdata.com/integrations/claude-code): one-command setup, project-scoped .mcp.json
- [Cursor](https://hasdata.com/integrations/cursor): one JSON block in ~/.cursor/mcp.json
- [Devin Desktop](https://hasdata.com/integrations/devin): Cascade config plus Devin CLI, the editor formerly called Windsurf
- [CLI](https://hasdata.com/integrations/cli): one static binary, JSON on stdout
- [OpenClaw](https://hasdata.com/integrations/openclaw): skill install, ask in the chat
- [Agent Skills](https://hasdata.com/integrations/agent-skills): npx skills add hasdata/agent-skills

